.TH LINUXCTL 1 "September 2026" "linux-mcp-daemon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linuxctl \- Command line interface for the Linux MCP Daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linuxctl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linuxctl
is the client utility for interacting with the Linux Model Context Protocol (MCP) Daemon (mcpd). It allows users and AI agents to send commands to the daemon running in the background.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-server \ \fIURL\fR
The URL of the mcpd server to connect to. Defaults to http://localhost:9090.
.TP
.BR \-token \ \fITOKEN\fR
Bearer token for authentication. If not provided via this flag, the client will look for the \fBMCP_TOKEN\fR environment variable.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ping
Pings the mcpd daemon to verify connectivity and authentication. Returns a success message if the daemon is reachable and the token is valid.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MCP_TOKEN
The bearer token used for authenticating with the daemon. Can be used instead of the \fB\-token\fR flag.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Ping the daemon using the default server and a specific token:
.IP
.B linuxctl \-token "my-test-token-123" ping
.PP
Ping the daemon using an environment variable:
.IP
.B export MCP_TOKEN="my-test-token-123"
.br
.B linuxctl ping
.SH AUTHOR
Antigravity
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcpd (8)
